       "t": "code",
       "lang": "python",
       "text": "from rclpy.node import Node\n\nclass MyFirstNode(Node):                    # inherit from ROS 2's Node class\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__('my_first_node')   # set up the node and name it\n        self.get_logger().info('Hello from my node!')"
      },
      {
       "t": "p",
       "text": "`Node` is a parent class written by the ROS 2 team. Your class inherits from it, so your node can do everything a node can do: log messages, publish, subscribe and use timers. `super().__init__('my_first_node')` runs Node's setup and gives your node its name."
      },
