    {
     "id": "A7",
     "title": "Environment variables, source and ~/.bashrc",
     "minutes": 25,
     "summary": "Why a new terminal forgets ROS 2, and how `source` and `~/.bashrc` fix it.",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "t": "story",
       "text": "Chiku forgets ROS 2 every time you open a new terminal. Let's fix that for good."
      },
      {
       "t": "p",
       "text": "Every terminal keeps a small set of settings called **environment variables**. Programs read them to learn things like your home folder or which ROS 2 version to use."
      },
      {
       "t": "code",
       "lang": "bash",
       "text": "echo $HOME                # /home/student\necho $ROS_DISTRO          # empty until ROS 2 is loaded\nexport ROBOT_NAME=chiku   # create a variable in this terminal\necho $ROBOT_NAME          # chiku\nprintenv | grep ROS       # show only variables containing ROS"
      },
      {
       "t": "analogy",
       "text": "A terminal is like a classroom whiteboard. `export` writes something on the board. Opening a **new** terminal is like walking into a new classroom with a clean board: everything written before is gone."
      },
      {
       "t": "h",
       "text": "Loading ROS 2 with source"
      },
      {
       "t": "p",
       "text": "ROS 2 is installed in `/opt/ros/jazzy`, but a new terminal does not know that. The command `source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash` writes all the ROS 2 settings on the board. Without it you get `ros2: command not found`."
      },
      {
       "t": "h",
       "text": "Making it automatic with ~/.bashrc"
      },
      {
       "t": "p",
       "text": "`~/.bashrc` is a hidden file that runs **every time** a new terminal opens. Add the source line to it once, and every new terminal loads ROS 2 by itself:"
      },
      {
       "t": "code",
       "lang": "bash",
       "text": "echo \"source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash\" >> ~/.bashrc"
      },
      {
       "t": "warn",
       "text": "Use **two** arrows, `>>`, which add a line at the end of the file. A single `>` replaces the whole file and erases your old settings."
      },
      {
       "t": "term",
       "title": "Practice: make ROS 2 load automatically",
       "newTerminal": true,
       "tasks": [
        {
         "do": "Try `ros2 topic list`. It fails, because ROS 2 is not loaded yet.",
         "check": {
          "cmd": "^ros2 topic list$"
         },
         "hint": "Type: ros2 topic list",
         "sol": "ros2 topic list"
        },
        {
         "do": "Load ROS 2 into this terminal: `source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash`",
         "check": {
          "sourced": true
         },
         "hint": "Type: source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash",
         "sol": "source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash"
        },
        {
         "do": "Check it: `echo $ROS_DISTRO` should print jazzy.",
         "check": {
          "cmd": "^echo \\$ROS_DISTRO$",
          "outputHas": "jazzy"
         },
         "hint": "Type: echo $ROS_DISTRO",
         "sol": "echo $ROS_DISTRO"
        },
        {
         "do": "Press **Open a new terminal** below, then type `echo $ROS_DISTRO` again. It is empty: the new terminal forgot.",
         "check": {
          "cmd": "^echo \\$ROS_DISTRO$",
          "sourced": false
         },
         "hint": "Click the \"Open a new terminal\" button, then type: echo $ROS_DISTRO",
         "sol": [
          {
           "newTerminal": true
          },
          "echo $ROS_DISTRO"
         ]
        },
        {
         "do": "Add the source line to `~/.bashrc`: `echo \"source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash\" >> ~/.bashrc`",
         "check": {
          "fileHas": {
           "path": "~/.bashrc",
           "text": "source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash"
          }
         },
         "hint": "Type it exactly, with the quotes and two arrows >>",
         "sol": "echo \"source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash\" >> ~/.bashrc"
        },
        {
         "do": "Open a new terminal again, then type `ros2 topic list`. It works now!",
         "check": {
          "cmd": "^ros2 topic list$",
          "sourced": true
         },
         "hint": "Click \"Open a new terminal\", then type: ros2 topic list",
         "sol": [
          {
           "newTerminal": true
          },
          "ros2 topic list"
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "t": "mcq",
       "q": "You opened a new terminal, and `ros2 run demo_nodes_py talker` says `ros2: command not found`. What do you type?",
       "options": [
        "source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash",
        "sudo ros2 run demo_nodes_py talker",
        "chmod +x ros2",
        "sudo apt update"
       ],
       "answer": 0,
       "why": "`source` loads ROS 2 into this terminal.",
       "hint": "The new terminal forgot ROS 2. Which command loads it?"
      },
      {
       "t": "mcq",
       "q": "Why do we add the source line to `~/.bashrc`?",
       "options": [
        "Because ~/.bashrc runs automatically every time a new terminal opens",
        "Because it makes the computer faster",
        "Because ROS 2 cannot be installed without it",
        "Because it deletes old settings"
       ],
       "answer": 0,
       "why": "Then every new terminal loads ROS 2 by itself.",
       "hint": "When does ~/.bashrc run?"
      },
      {
       "t": "fill",
       "q": "Type a command that prints the value of the variable `ROS_DISTRO`.",
       "accept": [
        "echo $ROS_DISTRO",
        "printenv ROS_DISTRO",
        "echo ${ROS_DISTRO}"
       ],
       "why": "`echo $NAME` prints a variable's value.",
       "hint": "echo, a space, then $ and the variable name."
      },
      {
       "t": "recap",
       "items": [
        "Environment variables are settings of one terminal. `export` creates one.",
        "New terminals start fresh. `source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash` loads ROS 2.",
        "Put the source line in `~/.bashrc` using `>>` to make it automatic."
       ]
      }
     ],
     "day": 10,
     "dayTitle": "Install ROS 2 and set up the lab"
    },
    {
     "id": "R4",
     "title": "Set up the ROS 2 robotics lab",
     "minutes": 45,
     "summary": "Install Gazebo, ros2_control, Nav2, SLAM, TurtleBot3 and MoveIt, prepare rosdep and a workspace, and check everything.",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "t": "story",
       "text": "Chiku is ready to graduate from the turtle simulator to real robot tools: **Gazebo** to simulate robots, **Nav2** to drive around a map, and **MoveIt** to move robot arms."
      },
      {
       "t": "goal",
       "items": [
        "Install the lab packages for mobile robots and robot arms",
        "Prepare rosdep and a colcon workspace",
        "Check everything with the lab checklist"
       ]
      },
      {
       "t": "words",
       "label": "What each tool is for",
       "items": [
        [
         "Gazebo Harmonic (ros-jazzy-ros-gz)",
         "the robot simulator, connected to ROS 2"
        ],
        [
         "ros2_control",
         "the standard way to drive motors and joints"
        ],
        [
         "Nav2",
         "lets a mobile robot plan a path and drive to a goal on a map"
        ],
        [
         "slam_toolbox / Cartographer",
         "build a map while the robot drives (SLAM)"
        ],
        [
         "TurtleBot3",
         "a small, popular teaching robot with ready-made simulations"
        ],
        [
         "MoveIt 2",
         "plans movements for robot arms without hitting things"
        ],
        [
         "colcon / rosdep",
         "build your own packages / install what they need"
        ]
       ]
      },
      {
       "t": "warn",
       "text": "ROS 2 Jazzy uses the **new Gazebo (Harmonic)**. Old tutorials that mention `gazebo_ros_pkgs`, Gazebo 11 or Gazebo Classic do not work on Jazzy."
      },
      {
       "t": "term",
       "title": "Dress rehearsal: set up the lab",
       "intro": "ROS 2 Jazzy is already installed in this practice terminal. Now add the lab tools.",
       "tasks": [
        {
         "do": "Install the build tools: `sudo apt install python3-colcon-common-extensions python3-rosdep`",
         "check": {
          "hasCmd": [
           "colcon",
           "rosdep"
          ]
         },
         "hint": "Type both package names after sudo apt install",
         "sol": "sudo apt install python3-colcon-common-extensions python3-rosdep"
        },
        {
         "do": "Set up rosdep once per computer: `sudo rosdep init`",
         "check": {
          "cmd": "^sudo rosdep init$"
         },
         "hint": "Type: sudo rosdep init",
         "sol": "sudo rosdep init"
        },
        {
         "do": "Update rosdep, **without** sudo: `rosdep update`",
         "check": {
          "rosdepUpdated": true
         },
         "hint": "Type: rosdep update",
         "sol": "rosdep update"
        },
        {
         "do": "Install Gazebo for ROS 2: `sudo apt install ros-jazzy-ros-gz`",
         "check": {
          "hasCmd": "gz"
         },
         "hint": "Type: sudo apt install ros-jazzy-ros-gz",
         "sol": "sudo apt install ros-jazzy-ros-gz"
        },
        {
         "do": "Install TurtleBot3: `sudo apt install 'ros-jazzy-turtlebot3*'` (with the quotes)",
         "check": {
          "rosPkg": "turtlebot3_gazebo"
         },
         "hint": "Type: sudo apt install 'ros-jazzy-turtlebot3*'",
         "sol": "sudo apt install 'ros-jazzy-turtlebot3*'"
        },
        {
         "do": "Install Nav2: `sudo apt install ros-jazzy-navigation2 ros-jazzy-nav2-bringup ros-jazzy-nav2-minimal-tb3-sim`",
         "check": {
          "rosPkg": [
           "nav2_bringup",
           "nav2_minimal_tb3_sim"
          ]
         },
         "hint": "Type the three package names after sudo apt install",
         "sol": "sudo apt install ros-jazzy-navigation2 ros-jazzy-nav2-bringup ros-jazzy-nav2-minimal-tb3-sim"
        },
        {
         "do": "Install MoveIt with the Panda arm demo: `sudo apt install ros-jazzy-moveit ros-jazzy-moveit-resources-panda-moveit-config`",
         "check": {
          "rosPkg": "moveit_resources_panda_moveit_config"
         },
         "hint": "Type both package names after sudo apt install",
         "sol": "sudo apt install ros-jazzy-moveit ros-jazzy-moveit-resources-panda-moveit-config"
        },
        {
         "do": "Load ROS 2 and choose the TurtleBot3 model: `source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash`, then `export TURTLEBOT3_MODEL=burger`",
         "check": {
          "sourced": true,
          "env": {
           "TURTLEBOT3_MODEL": "burger"
          }
         },
         "hint": "Two commands: source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash  then  export TURTLEBOT3_MODEL=burger",
         "sol": [
          "source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash",
          "export TURTLEBOT3_MODEL=burger"
         ]
        },
        {
         "do": "Start TurtleBot3 in Gazebo: `ros2 launch turtlebot3_gazebo turtlebot3_world.launch.py`",
         "check": {
          "cmd": "^ros2 launch turtlebot3_gazebo turtlebot3_world\\.launch\\.py$",
          "outputHas": "process started"
         },
         "hint": "Type: ros2 launch turtlebot3_gazebo turtlebot3_world.launch.py",
         "sol": "ros2 launch turtlebot3_gazebo turtlebot3_world.launch.py"
        },
        {
         "do": "Start the robot-arm demo: `ros2 launch moveit_resources_panda_moveit_config demo.launch.py`",
         "check": {
          "cmd": "^ros2 launch moveit_resources_panda_moveit_config demo\\.launch\\.py$",
          "outputHas": "move_group"
         },
         "hint": "Type: ros2 launch moveit_resources_panda_moveit_config demo.launch.py",
         "sol": "ros2 launch moveit_resources_panda_moveit_config demo.launch.py"
        },
        {
         "do": "Make and build a workspace: `mkdir -p ~/ros2_ws/src`, `cd ~/ros2_ws`, then `colcon build`",
         "check": {
          "dir": "~/ros2_ws/install"
         },
         "hint": "Three commands: mkdir -p ~/ros2_ws/src, cd ~/ros2_ws, colcon build",
         "sol": [
          "mkdir -p ~/ros2_ws/src",
          "cd ~/ros2_ws",
          "colcon build"
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "t": "h",
       "text": "Now on your real computer"
      },
      {
       "t": "p",
       "text": "Run these commands one by one on your Ubuntu 24.04 with ROS 2 Jazzy installed. Together they download a few gigabytes."
      },
      {
       "t": "code",
       "lang": "bash",
       "text": "sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y\nsudo apt install -y python3-colcon-common-extensions python3-rosdep python3-vcstool\nsudo rosdep init\nrosdep update\nsudo apt install -y ros-jazzy-robot-state-publisher ros-jazzy-joint-state-publisher-gui ros-jazzy-xacro ros-jazzy-tf2-tools ros-jazzy-teleop-twist-keyboard 'ros-jazzy-rqt*'\nsudo apt install -y ros-jazzy-ros-gz\nsudo apt install -y ros-jazzy-ros2-control ros-jazzy-ros2-controllers ros-jazzy-gz-ros2-control ros-jazzy-gz-ros2-control-demos\nsudo apt install -y ros-jazzy-navigation2 ros-jazzy-nav2-bringup 'ros-jazzy-nav2-minimal-tb*' ros-jazzy-slam-toolbox ros-jazzy-robot-localization ros-jazzy-cartographer-ros 'ros-jazzy-turtlebot3*'\nsudo apt install -y ros-jazzy-moveit ros-jazzy-moveit-resources-panda-moveit-config ros-jazzy-ur-description",
       "copy": true
      },
      {
       "t": "p",
       "text": "Then add your lab settings to `~/.bashrc`, so every new terminal is ready:"
      },
      {
       "t": "code",
       "lang": "bash",
       "text": "echo \"source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash\" >> ~/.bashrc\necho \"export TURTLEBOT3_MODEL=burger\" >> ~/.bashrc\necho \"export ROS_DOMAIN_ID=7\" >> ~/.bashrc\nsource ~/.bashrc",
       "copy": true
      },
      {
       "t": "tip",
       "text": "In the lab, every student uses a **different** `ROS_DOMAIN_ID` (a number from 0 to 101, given by your instructor), so your robot doesn't listen to your neighbour's commands. Real TurtleBot3 robots in the lab are set up by the instructor following the ROBOTIS e-Manual for Jazzy."
      },
      {
       "t": "checklist",
       "title": "Lab-ready checklist (on your real computer)",
       "items": [
        "`printenv ROS_DISTRO` prints `jazzy`",
        "Talker and listener talk: `ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp talker` and, in a second terminal, `ros2 run demo_nodes_py listener`",
        "Turtlesim moves: `ros2 run turtlesim turtlesim_node` and `ros2 run turtlesim turtle_teleop_key`",
        "Gazebo opens: `gz sim shapes.sdf`",
        "TurtleBot3 drives in Gazebo: `ros2 launch turtlebot3_gazebo turtlebot3_world.launch.py`, then `ros2 run teleop_twist_keyboard teleop_twist_keyboard` in a second terminal",
        "Nav2 reaches a goal: `ros2 launch nav2_bringup tb3_simulation_launch.py headless:=False`, then 2D Pose Estimate and Nav2 Goal in RViz",
        "MoveIt plans a motion: `ros2 launch moveit_resources_panda_moveit_config demo.launch.py`, then Plan & Execute in RViz",
        "My workspace builds: `cd ~/ros2_ws && colcon build`"
       ]
      },
      {
       "t": "h",
       "text": "Reading errors calmly"
      },
      {
       "t": "list",
       "items": [
        "`Package '...' not found`: install it with apt (the apt name uses dashes: `ros-jazzy-...`), then source again.",
        "`KeyError: 'TURTLEBOT3_MODEL'` or `Caught exception ... 'TURTLEBOT3_MODEL'`: run `export TURTLEBOT3_MODEL=burger`.",
        "`ros2: command not found`: run `source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash`.",
        "Your robot moves when your neighbour presses keys: set a different `ROS_DOMAIN_ID`.",
        "Read the **last line** of an error first. It usually says what is wrong in plain words."
       ]
      },
      {
       "t": "mcq",
       "q": "Which package connects ROS 2 Jazzy to the Gazebo Harmonic simulator?",
       "options": [
        "ros-jazzy-ros-gz",
        "ros-jazzy-gazebo-ros-pkgs",
        "gazebo11",
        "ros-jazzy-turtlesim"
       ],
       "answer": 0,
       "why": "Jazzy uses the new Gazebo through ros_gz; Gazebo Classic packages don't exist for Jazzy.",
       "hint": "Look for gz."
      },
      {
       "t": "mcq",
       "q": "A TurtleBot3 launch file stops with an error about `'TURTLEBOT3_MODEL'`. What is the fix?",
       "options": [
        "export TURTLEBOT3_MODEL=burger",
        "sudo apt update",
        "sudo rosdep init",
        "chmod +x the launch file"
       ],
       "answer": 0,
       "why": "The TurtleBot3 launch files read the robot model from that variable.",
       "hint": "The error names a variable."
      },
      {
       "t": "mcq",
       "q": "Where do you run `colcon build`?",
       "options": [
        "In the workspace folder, for example ~/ros2_ws",
        "Inside ~/ros2_ws/src",
        "In /opt/ros/jazzy",
        "In the Desktop folder"
       ],
       "answer": 0,
       "why": "colcon build runs in the workspace folder and creates build, install and log next to src.",
       "hint": "Not inside src."
      },
      {
       "t": "tip",
       "label": "Week 2 test",
       "text": "When you have finished all Week 2 lessons, the **Week 2 test** unlocks on your course page."
      },
      {
       "t": "recap",
       "items": [
